# The store is a LOCAL BUILD ARTIFACT. context/memory-graph.dump is the tracked
# source of truth; the database is rebuilt from it automatically on open (sync.py).
# Never track the .db: git cannot auto-register a clean/smudge filter, so a tracked
# binary either arrives as un-openable text or poisons history as raw SQLite.
context/memory-graph.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db.bak

# Build output (uv build + scripts/build-assets.py)
/dist/

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Tooling workspaces (regenerated locally; not tracked)
.serena/
graphify-out/

# GUI build output — a build artifact, rebuilt with `npm run build` in gui/
# (locally via `make dist`, and in CI on release). Not tracked, so a fresh clone
# must build the GUI before agentic-memory-gui can serve it.
gui/node_modules/
gui/dist/
